+
+## Native Google Sign-In for Android clients (2026-09-21)
+
+`POST /api/auth/native/google` — added. The Android apps (`EnJirad/velnox-app`) cannot
+use the browser OAuth flow (a Custom Tab cannot hand back cookies; an embedded WebView is
+blocked by Google), so they obtain a Google ID token via Credential Manager and exchange
+it here.
+
+- **Reuses** `verifyGoogleIdentity` and `resolveUser` verbatim — no second identity
+  resolution path, so `auth_identities (provider, provider_id)` → normalised `users.email`
+  → create still holds: one person, one row, no duplicate accounts.
+- Responds with the same JWT the browser receives in the `velnox_session` cookie, **and**
+  returns it in the body (`data.token`) because a native client stores it itself.
+- `setSessionCookie` is called too, so per-user rate limiting and the WebSocket handshake
+  see a native session exactly as they see a browser one.
+
+`verifyGoogleIdentity` was hardened to check every claim it relies on rather than only the
+audience: signature via `tokeninfo`, **audience** (`aud === GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`), **issuer**
+(`accounts.google.com` / `https://accounts.google.com`), **expiry** (explicit, not inferred
+from `tokeninfo`'s status code) and an optional **nonce** echoed by Google. Rejections now
+throw `GoogleTokenError` with a code (`INVALID_GOOGLE_TOKEN`, `GOOGLE_AUDIENCE_MISMATCH`,
+`GOOGLE_ISSUER_MISMATCH`, `GOOGLE_TOKEN_EXPIRED`, `GOOGLE_NONCE_MISMATCH`) which the route
+returns as 401 + that code, so the client can tell a bad token from a server fault. The
+browser callback passes no nonce and is otherwise unchanged.
+
+`POST /api/auth/member-login` now also returns `token` + `expiresInSeconds` in its body.
+The web client ignores them and keeps using the cookie; without them the Android VelCenter
+sign-in received a valid session it could not see.
+
+**No schema change** — the nonce is verified against the token's own claim, not stored, so
+`db/schema.sql` and `db/run-sqleditor.sql` are untouched and remain byte-identical.
+
+### Not verified here
+
+No deployment. The endpoint exists in source and passes `tsc --noEmit` plus
+`bun test backend/tests` (351 pass / 0 fail), but it is **not live** until this is
+deployed to Render and `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` matches the client id the Android build embeds.
