 ## Source Locations
 
-- `backend/routes/auth.ts` — `GET /auth/google`, `GET /auth/google/callback`, `GET /api/auth/me`, `POST /api/auth/logout`
+- `backend/routes/auth.ts` — `GET /auth/google`, `GET /auth/google/callback`, `POST /api/auth/native/google`, `POST /api/auth/member-login`, `GET /api/auth/me`, `POST /api/auth/logout`, `POST /api/auth/change-password`
+
+### Native clients (Android)
+
+A Custom Tab cannot hand its cookies back to an app and an embedded WebView is
+blocked by Google, so the Android clients obtain a **Google ID token** through
+Credential Manager and post it to `POST /api/auth/native/google` with the OIDC
+`nonce` they requested. That endpoint reuses `verifyGoogleIdentity` and
+`resolveUser` unchanged, so identity resolution — and therefore account linking —
+is identical to the browser flow, then returns the same JWT the cookie carries.
+`verifyGoogleIdentity` checks signature (tokeninfo), audience, issuer, expiry and
+the nonce, and refuses a request without one. `member-login` also returns its
+token in the body for the same reason.
 - `backend/middleware/auth.ts` — `requireAuth`, `optionalAuth`, JWT verify, `revoked_tokens` check (in-memory `revokedJTIs` set + DB fallback)
 - `backend/db/index.ts` — `revoked_tokens` table
 - `packages/shared/src/hooks/use-auth.ts`, `packages/shared/src/components/RequireAuth.tsx`, `packages/shared/src/components/RequireRole.tsx` — frontend auth state
